text:
This place doesn't  deserve the 1 star that others gave for some out of the box reasons  ... In my opinion This is a 4 star place; nice smell inside, good coffee, good service, clean, not loud... Everything you can want from a coffee shop; 

The reason i gave 4 starts is because of the seatings; i want a comfy seat, soft, cozy :) ( they have a few but they need more; they also have a big nice sofa , but only one :(  ) but this is just my opinion;
Enjoy the coffee here

Newer, more spacious location compared to its State Street counterpart.

They serve and sell Verve coffee beans. 

// PARKING // Small lot on the property for a quick stop for coffee.

// SERVICE // The baristas were a bit backed up, but all of the workers were cheery and helpful

// FOOD //
     + Shakerato: Two shots of expresso with simple syrup shaken in a shaker and poured over ice. As bold and enjoyable as the other location. It is a quick pick me up that will jolt you awake.
     + Vanilla latte: The vanilla was very fragrant and I asked them to only put in 1/2 the amount of vanilla. It was the perfect amount of sweetness and did not taste artificial at all. It was a good balance with the espresso and milk (You can customize the milk upon request-Soy, non-fat, almond, etc).

//fresh micro roasted coffee in a friendly atmosphere
//you'll appreciate if you enjoy Blue Bottle, Four Barrel, Intelligentsia, Stumptown
//tasty pastries to compliment the coffee
//simple coffee menu-no frapachinnos here

Handlebar is another great coffee location in downtown Santa Barbara and is a favorite for many bikers. I loved the hip and earthy vibe of the place complete with funky fonts and a giant coffee roaster.

// SERVICE // The woman (who I believe may be the owner) was incredibly sweet, welcoming, and informative. She told me the store makes their own vanilla and chocolate syrup to flavor the coffees. The employees are much more welcoming and warm than those at the French Press.

// FOOD // 
     + Vanilla latte: I asked her to only put a tiny bit of vanilla into the latte which she happily obliged. The latte was very hot and the hint of vanilla was very fragrant and lightly sweetened the drink.
     + Cappuccino: Complete with pretty foam art! We sweetened it a bit with the cane sugar available. It was bold which was balanced with the foam.

Tasty tasty bakery in Downtown Santa Barbara

// LOCATION // Arlington Plaza

// PARKING // Plenty of parking in the lot (shared with other businesses) or on the street

// SERVICE // Sweet workers who explained the items to us.

// FOOD // 
     + Almond croissant: Scrumptious, especially after the worker heated and plated it for us. The crust was buttery and glazed with a thin layer of sliced almonds and sugar. It was the perfect sweet snack after any meal

*tip: Renaud's pastries are also sold at the Handlebar Coffee shop

Great hip coffee with two locations in Santa Barbara. They use Verve coffee beans from Santa Cruz. 

// PARKING // Street or public lots. 

// FOOD // 
     + Shakerato: Had to try their famous drink. 2 shots of espresso shaken in a shaker with ice and simple syrup. It is served in a small cappuccino cup over some ice. It is very bold without being too strong. If you are someone who likes to sip on a drink for a long time though, this is not for you because it is about half a capuccino cup max in terms of quantity. 
    + Iced coffee with soy milk: Creamy with bold coffee flavor. Reminiscent of Joe's Coffee in NYC

*Their other location has a small parking lot.

Pleasant and cozy shop with friendly baristas and a killer "Red Eye". This shop is my first choice on State and I've never been disappointed yet.

I would definitely recommend this shop and remember;

"Coffee should be served black as the night, hotter than Hell and sweeter than a womans' heart.."

I was looking forward to the Dim Sum with my wife and daughter, I've heard some good things about the restaurant.

Cons;
It was one of the poorest service I've received.  It was quite awhile before any of the employees asked if we were ready.  Maybe I've been spoiled by other dim sum locations.  We were wondering if we were missing something.  We were never checked up upon after we finally placed our order.  We finally got our bill and at least one refill of our water.

Pros;
The food was fine.  I would give it 3.5 stars and definite a bit tastier than most other Chinese restaurants I've encountered in Santa Barbara.  That being said I will probably not return.  I think I will stick with the restaurants I normally patronize.

Can't speak to the food; 
after a 25 minute wait on-line outside in the sun, without being seated, and despite a heatwave- this "classy joint" refused a glass of water to those waiting on line;
we decided to try out another local breakfast joint.
OH: and despite advertising as offering "all day breakfast" the only option after they switch to lunch service at 11:30 am...?  is what they call the all day breakfast: two eggs, toast, and - french fries!

???

Yes - you can't even get breakfast potatoes with your "all day breakfast"
